WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.542
In 1937, the morning at Lugou Bridge was still quiet.

00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:07.603
After the incident, full-scale war broke out between China and Japan.

00:00:07.603 --> 00:00:11.180
The stone lions on the bridge gazed quietly at the river.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.355
Many people packed their belongings and left their homes.

00:00:15.355 --> 00:00:19.030
Supporting the old and carrying the young, they headed to unfamiliar places.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.371
Children clung tightly to their mothers' hands, refusing to let go.

00:00:22.371 --> 00:00:25.697
Bustling streets became completely empty.

00:00:25.697 --> 00:00:28.981
Shop doors were shut tight, with only wind-blown leaves remaining.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:33.030
People crossed mountains and ridges in search of safety.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.543
Schools and factories also moved westward.

00:00:36.543 --> 00:00:40.277
In their new places, children returned to classrooms.

00:00:40.277 --> 00:00:43.679
The war lasted eight years, and life was very hard.

00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:46.493
But people did not give up on learning and living.

00:00:46.493 --> 00:00:50.060
Everyone helped each other to get through the hard times.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:53.646
In 1945, Japan announced its surrender.

00:00:53.646 --> 00:00:56.771
The war finally ended, and people embraced in the streets.
